Arcadium & Circadia (AuraEngine / Sesephus Suite)
An offline-first, high-performance background alarm engine and audio processing daemon written in Zig (v0.16.0), bridged with a Python FastAPI AI transcription layer and a premium React + Vite web dashboard.

Arcadium & Circadia (historically envisioned as AuraEngine or the Sesephus Suite) is designed for local-first audio journaling and behavioral therapy management (e.g., CBT/DBT diary cards, scheduled checkpoints, habit cues, and ambient logging).

🌌 System Architecture & Modernized Design
Our architecture enforces a clean separation of concerns by utilizing Zig for low-level systems execution and network reliability, Python for local AI inference (transcription), and React/Vite for a premium web user interface.

Mermaid diagram
1. 🕰️ Circadia & Arcadium: The Zig Daemons (core/sesephus/)
The native core of the engine is written in pure Zig (v0.16.0), requiring zero external runtime dependencies and utilizing Win32 multimedia APIs (winmm.dll waveIn interface):

Circadia (The Alarm Engine): A priority-queue-based scheduler managing alarms across client devices. Communicates over a custom TCP client/host architecture using length-prefixed protocol frames.
Arcadium (Audio Journaling Engine): Captures audio on client devices using low-latency APIs (or a synthetic sine-wave generator fallback for headless hosts) and pipes WAV data over TCP.
Encrypted Vault: The Zig Host daemon ingests incoming WAV data into an encrypted local database vault (sesephus_vault.db) using ChaCha20-Poly1305 authenticated encryption (AEAD) with key derivation via PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256.
2. 🎙️ Python AI Bridge (dashboard/dashboard_server.py)
AI inference pipelines (such as whisper) are complex to run in pure Zig. Python acts as our dedicated AI bridge:

Runs a lightweight FastAPI server on port 3001.
Manages local transcription of uploaded WAV journals using OpenAI's Whisper.
Updates local task lists and telemetry stores.
Polls the Zig Host (http://localhost:3000/api/status) dynamically to track connected client state, completely eliminating the need for a heavy NATS message broker.
3. 🎨 Unified Web Dashboard (dashboard/ui/)
A unified Vite + React dashboard that presents a premium, zero-bloat dark-mode and glassmorphism interface:

Styled using pure Vanilla CSS (index.css) for high performance and zero framework overhead.
Uses Vite's development proxy to forward frontend /api requests to the Python sidecar on port 3001, avoiding CORS issues entirely.
📁 Workspace Directory Guide
The workspace is organized into domain-specific modules:

core/sesephus/: Low-level Zig system daemons (Host & Client). Handles TCP networking, the encrypted vault (sesephus_vault.db), and raw alarm triggers.
dashboard/: User interfaces and sidecar servers. Contains the FastAPI sidecar (dashboard_server.py) and the unified Vite + React frontend (dashboard/ui).
ingest/: Active database and ingestion shards storing raw code/text chunks (debris_shards.jsonl) and 768-dimensional mathematical coordinates (vector_shards.jsonl).
aurgio/: Local voice journals, transcript metadata, and raw audio files.
audio/: Edge capturing scripts, FFT analyzers, and audio processing tools.
shredder/: Sieve text-shredding and redaction modules.
simulator/: Agentic conversation emulators and broker simulators for testing logic.
client/: Standalone audio capturer experiments (recorder.zig).
tools/: Support utilities and system scripts (e.g., compress_archive.zig).
utils/: Chat pruners, latent space noise filters (spiffy_prune.py), and prompt compression scripts.
venv/: Local Python virtual environment housing FastAPI, Uvicorn, Pydantic, and Whisper dependencies.
docs/: Reference guides, backups, and CLI log archives.
⚙️ Getting Started
1. Build the Zig Core
Navigate to the core directory and build the binaries:

bash

cd core/sesephus
zig build -Doptimize=ReleaseSafe
This generates host.exe and client.exe in zig-out/bin/.

2. Start the Python AI Sidecar
Set up dependencies (FastAPI, Uvicorn, Pydantic, Whisper) and launch the sidecar server:

bash

# In the repository root
venv\Scripts\python.exe dashboard/dashboard_server.py
The FastAPI sidecar will start on http://127.0.0.1:3001.

3. Run the React Web Dashboard
Navigate to the UI directory, install dependencies, and run the Vite dev server:

bash

cd dashboard/ui
npm install
npm run dev
Open http://localhost:5173 to interact with the premium unified dashboard.

4. Running the Complete System Demo
You can run the interactive demo using the automated script:

cmd

core\sesephus\run_demo.bat
This builds the Zig binaries, spawns the Host Daemon and Client Device in separate windows, and prompts you to schedule and trigger interactive alarms.

🚴 Therapeutic Finite State Machine (FSM)
AuraEngine models journaling sessions as a state-driven FSM to guide users through therapeutic protocols:

State	Description	Next State
Idle	System is waiting for the next scheduled cue.	Prompting
Prompting	Plays auditory tone and displays therapeutic prompt.	Breathing / Recording
Breathing	Guide user through paced breathing (ambient sounds).	Recording
Recording	Captures spoken journal response (encodes to WAV/Opus).	Reflecting
Reflecting	Prompts user to label emotions and self-assess mood.	Saving
Saving	Writes compressed audio and metadata locally.	Idle
📜 Key Architectural Revelations
Local-First Simplicity: Removing enterprise technologies like NATS streamlined the system footprint. Standard HTTP API polling from FastAPI to the Zig Host is faster, less error-prone, and runs locally out-of-the-box.
Zig as the Source of Truth: The Zig Host Daemon manages the active socket state and databases directly, acting as the system's central authority, while Python acts purely as a stateless utility bridge for AI inference.
Low-Latency and Memory Safety: High-priority audio threads on the edge clients use strict zero-allocation patterns to guarantee glitch-free captures.
